                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Watches the live residuals while the run is going; once every field's residual has been flat for about 100 iterations after any warm-up ramp, writes stopAt=writeNow — exactly what the manual right-click 'Stop Simulation Gracefully' action does — so the solver finishes its current iteration, writes the latest fields, and exits cleanly instead of grinding out the rest of the iteration count. Requires a Live Residuals component monitoring the case. Optional; default is off.</item>
