            <chunk name="Object" index="28">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">3fbc22c8-fa0f-465a-a696-a2878fc05385</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">ABL APPROACH-FLOW VERIFICATION
ASCE/SEI CWE Prestandard PO 4-1 / AC 4-1.
Units: METERS.

WHAT THIS CHECKS: does the atmospheric boundary
layer imposed at the inlet still exist by the
time it reaches the buildings? Every wind study
assumes it does; the Prestandard makes checking
it a required step before the building run.

TWO VERTICAL RAKES on the canyon centreline
(y = 60), 16 points each from Series:
2.5 m to 77.5 m in 5 m steps.
  x = 0   the approach flow near the inlet
  x = 40  the upwind face of the buildings
Compare the two profiles. Probe Field is "U".
That series contains all six heights the fixture
rakes (2.5 / 7.5 / 17.5 / 32.5 / 52.5 / 77.5),
which are cell centres of ITS 5 m z-mesh.

ABL: 5 m/s at 10 m reference height, z0 = 1 m -
the three numbers TestAblSelfSustainmentContainer
E2E writes its analytic log law against.
Iterations 400, the fixture's count.

*** SCOPE LIMIT - READ THIS ***
The Prestandard asks for an EMPTY domain. That
cannot be built here: OutdoorCaseCMP returns
early with "Connect at least one closed building
mesh to the Buildings input", so no Case object
is produced without geometry. This template
therefore rakes the REAL domain, which answers
"has the profile decayed by the building
position" but not the standard's empty-domain
form.

The fixture's own stations (y = 5 / 105 / 195 in
a 100 x 200 x 100 m empty box) belong to that
empty domain and do not transfer to this site.

A decay here is EXPECTED, not a bug: the log-law
ABL solves OpenFOAM's epsilon equation only at
sigmaEps = 1.1674, and stock kEpsilon runs 1.3.
The point is to see how big it is.

Automating the AC 5-9 error integral
(eps_ABL-U &lt;= 0.1) is feature F2 in
docs/ASCE-CWE-PRESTANDARD-COMPLIANCE.md and does
not ship. Nothing here computes it.

Action toggles ship OFF.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>1870</X>
                          <Y>165</Y>
                          <W>423</W>
                          <H>268</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="MarginLeft" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="MarginRight" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="MarginTop" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="PanelProperties">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Colour" type_name="gh_drawing_color" type_code="36">
                          <ARGB>255;255;250;90</ARGB>
                        </item>
                        <item name="DrawIndices" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="DrawPaths" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="Multiline" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SpecialCodes" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Stream" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Wrap" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                  </chunks>
                </chunk>
              </chunks>
            </chunk>
            <chunk name="Object" index="29">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e64c5fb1-845c-4ab1-8911-5f338516ba67</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Series</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
